    "journalReadings": {
      "note": "Every non-zero AmmoInClip / AmmoInHopper across the ten journal captures — the only external readings of `clipSize` and `ammoMaximum` this repository holds. All forty-two sit exactly at capacity, on eighteen distinct modules, several of which appear in more than one capture. A reading is still only a lower bound on what a module holds, and must never be read back as a catalogue figure: a journal's ammunition is the ship's rearm state at the instant of capture, so a partly spent launcher would report less than its capacity and say nothing about the catalogue. The Lynx Highliner's heat-sink launcher is the case that shows why the bound has to hold both ways — it reports 3 in reserve under a grade-1 Heat Sink Capacity, against a base of 2, so a capacity read straight off it would be the engineered figure. On the Corsair the capacity is likewise the engineered one, since three of its five ammunition-bearing weapons carry an `AmmoClipSize` or `AmmoMaximum` modifier; the two plasma accelerators take Long Range, which charges neither. The Corvette's large gimballed cannon sits at capacity under a grade-5 Overcharged, which is Frontier's own reading that the recipe does not cut a cannon's clip — a 15% penalty would have loaded four rounds. That reading is evidence and not a guard: a build parsed from a journal folds the modifiers the journal states, so adding a clip leg to the recipe would not move these counts. What fails on such a change is the engineering suite, which folds the recipe itself.",
